+    also: core/components/plays/understand/reference/ice.md
+    principle: "Inside a drive a config skip is recorded as a skip, as by hand, and only a would-wait gate becomes a review record. A play's evals must judge the same cases its steps produce. And because /understand writes box-move decisions as proposed, the drive's review has to be able to find every one of them."
+    source: "main:core/components/memory/standards/rules/drive-contract.md ('How a play runs inside a drive' item 3); main:core/components/memory/standards/rules/gate-config.md (config skip and ledger lines); main:core/components/plays/vision/SKILL.md SE-14 (same wording, the precedent this inherits)"
+    detail: >
+      SKILL.md Step 6 (drive paragraph) and ice C13 say a config skip is 'recorded as a skip' and the review
+      record is written only 'where the gate resolves ON'. SE-16 (and S7's measure) then say 'when the gate did
