+    path: core/components/plays/understand/reference/ice.md
+    also: core/components/plays/understand/SKILL.md
+    principle: "Each play shows its saved record, one /understand record per capability, so the drive's review can tell them apart."
+    source: "main:docs/adr/029-drives.md section 6 ('Done when': 'one /understand record per capability'); main:core/components/memory/standards/rules/drive-contract.md ('drive_run_id ... so the drive's review can find each play's record')"
+    detail: >
+      C13, S7 and SE-16 say each run leaves its own record at <review_dir>/understand-<ts>.json. The canonical
+      writer names the file by play and timestamp only and records no capability; the capability shows only
+      inside the summary and the attachment paths. Two runs started in the same second would overwrite each
+      other, and a reader of the JSON cannot tell which capability it is. Have the play put the capability in
