+  - id: H7
+    category: harness
+    severity: P4
+    title: "F14 and REC14 call a by-hand run that 'skipped its checkpoint' a failure, though a config skip or learned auto-pass legitimately skips it"
+    path: core/components/plays/understand/reference/ice.md
+    principle: "Run by hand, a play still stops as its gate settings say; a config skip and a policy auto-pass are valid resolutions of a conditional gate."
+    source: "main:docs/adr/029-drives.md section 4 and 'ADRs This Retires' (002 in part); main:core/components/memory/standards/rules/gate-config.md"
+    detail: >
+      F14's tail: 'run by hand, it skipped its opening, its checkpoint or its end sequence'; REC14: 'by hand, run
